This is a Python project that generates investor-ready PPTX slide decks
for a hedge fund.

Architecture:
- src/data_loader.py: CSV/Excel ingestion + Yahoo Finance price enrichment
- src/analytics.py: Portfolio analytics (returns, risk, exposure, attribution)
- src/chart_generator.py: Matplotlib charts rendered as PNG to charts/
- src/slide_builder.py: python-pptx deck assembly
- generate_deck.py: CLI entry point with argparse
- config/fund_config.yaml: All branding, colours, fonts, slide toggles

Conventions:
- All colours MUST come from fund_config.yaml — never hardcode hex values in slide_builder or chart_generator
- Charts are saved as PNG to charts/ then embedded into slides as images
- Every new slide type needs a boolean toggle in fund_config.yaml under slides:
- Use Python type hints on all function signatures
- Holdings DataFrame columns after enrichment: ticker, quantity, avg_cost, currency, sector, country, strategy_sleeve, side, current_price, market_value, cost_basis, weight_gross, pnl, pnl_pct
- Slide dimensions: 13.333" x 7.5" (widescreen)
- python-pptx for slides, NOT pptxgenjs
- Keep modules independent — data_loader knows nothing about slides, chart_generator knows nothing about analytics logic
